{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>For you shall come with this people.</b> \"אֲרֵי אַתְּ תֵעוּל עִם עַמָּא הָדֵין\" — Moses said to Joshua: elders of the generation shall be with you, everything according to their understanding and counsel. But the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Joshua: \"כִּי אַתָּה תָּבִיא אֶת בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶל הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר נִשְׁבַּעְתִּי לָהֶם\" — you shall bring them against their will; everything depends on you. Take a staff and strike them on the head — one matter for a generation, not two matters for a generation (Sanhedrin 8)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "The Aramaic quotation is Onkelos's rendering of the verse, which Rashi cites to distinguish 'coming with the people' (Moses' charge) from 'bringing the people' (HaShem's charge to Joshua)."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:01.187978503Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}